                "word": "desultory",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c5dd1de7-df6d-4295-8ba0-eac933454451",
                        "entry_id": "f14913a2-e1c8-357c-9078-cef37add95b2",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more desultory"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "d53a4a70-8fdb-4866-9b0d-6d5d51c920d0",
                        "entry_id": "f14913a2-e1c8-357c-9078-cef37add95b2",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most desultory"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8ffa3b7d-ab9a-300a-bb41-041490cc364e",
                        "entry_id": "f14913a2-e1c8-357c-9078-cef37add95b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Jumping, or passing, from one thing or subject to another, without order, planning, or rational connection; lacking logical sequence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9bbd23a-55d7-4f9d-8fb9-c03522633f86",
                                "sense_id": "8ffa3b7d-ab9a-300a-bb41-041490cc364e",
                                "text": "He wandered round, cleaning up in a desultory way."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b363f29-b80b-4bfb-9a4c-dd80d6487572",
                                "sense_id": "8ffa3b7d-ab9a-300a-bb41-041490cc364e",
                                "text": "I teach a class of desultory minds."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "feff5ad2-224c-44cd-8fd0-078f31eab495",
                                "sense_id": "8ffa3b7d-ab9a-300a-bb41-041490cc364e",
                                "text": "subject to desultory fire from the enemy"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "71f9a2a2-9cb5-4a6c-b4ca-ad00ac08027d",
                                "sense_id": "8ffa3b7d-ab9a-300a-bb41-041490cc364e",
                                "text": "To mend the matter, Hamlet's aunt had the family failing of indulging in soliloquy, and held forth in a desultory manner, by herself, on every topic that was introduced."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "88a4a5ba-63d1-4703-88d4-245e74d106c5",
                                "sense_id": "8ffa3b7d-ab9a-300a-bb41-041490cc364e",
                                "text": "The Benelux Customs Union came into effect on January 1st 1948, and there followed desultory conversations between the Benelux countries, France and Italy over projects to extend such cooperation across a larger space."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b1d71ae-229d-4b76-af90-af4725f58b9a",
                                "sense_id": "8ffa3b7d-ab9a-300a-bb41-041490cc364e",
                                "text": "‘Your desultory twenties,’ my mother calls my lost time, trying to make it sound reasonable and fun, but it started before I was twenty and lasted much longer."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9273d5d4-69f1-3a25-aefa-9fabe2a50205",
                        "entry_id": "f14913a2-e1c8-357c-9078-cef37add95b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Out of course; by the way; not connected with the subject."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b440ca76-c02a-4a43-973f-38bf2bde7dc4",
                                "sense_id": "9273d5d4-69f1-3a25-aefa-9fabe2a50205",
                                "text": "I made a desultory remark while I was talking to my friend."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7f8f5a36-0809-4081-8fdc-d85a8f91529e",
                                "sense_id": "9273d5d4-69f1-3a25-aefa-9fabe2a50205",
                                "text": "She made a desultory attempt at conversation."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2e0b3777-8001-39eb-ae6c-7fb4fcd89c33",
                        "entry_id": "f14913a2-e1c8-357c-9078-cef37add95b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Disappointing in performance or progress."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "23cb901e-172a-40a5-9004-80dcf6896577",
                                "sense_id": "2e0b3777-8001-39eb-ae6c-7fb4fcd89c33",
                                "text": "As we stood waiting for the departure time with the setting sun twinkling on the great brass dome of our 2-4-0, the sound of church bells was the only one apart from the measured tread of the guard slowly pacing towards his van, and, standing at an open window, I more than once heard the fireman's \"Right away!\" to his mate in acknowledgement of a desultory wave of the unfurled green flag."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "46038589-34d4-34f7-ac79-92b4ed8f9f96",
                        "entry_id": "f14913a2-e1c8-357c-9078-cef37add95b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Leaping, skipping or flitting about, generally in a random or unsteady manner."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
